questions.question:
A test in the CodeDev API (Vitest 3.x) freezes the clock before checking the "due today" banner:

vi.useFakeTimers();
vi.setSystemTime(new Date("2026-11-01T06:30:00+07:00"));
const day = new Date().getDate();

The test passes on a developer laptop in Hanoi (time zone Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh). The CI runner's time zone is UTC.

Statement: "Because the system time is frozen, day is 1 on the laptop and on the CI runner."

After the fix, submissionStatus(assignment, clock) reads the time only from clock.now(). A teammate updates the old test like this:

test("a submission before today's deadline is on time", () => {
  const now = new Date();
  const today = now.toISOString().slice(0, 10);
  const quiz = { id: "ts-quiz-3", deadline: `${today}T23:59`, utcOffsetMinutes: 420, graceMinutes: 15 };
  expect(submissionStatus(quiz, { now: () => now })).toBe("on-time");
});

Statement: "This test can still fail when the nightly CI run starts at 01:30 Vietnam time."
